From 1747a56f89113b8e2900da8e411703025408ea99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kumar-Jy <20044626+Kumar-Jy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 01 Sep 2026 15:36:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150-xiaomi-nabu: only advertise
 5V sink PDO

The SMB5 charger block only charges reliably from a 5V input.  The
PDO_VAR(5000, 9000, 3000) sink PDO lets USB-PD sources negotiate 9V
(or other voltages in range), and although PD negotiation succeeds the
battery then never charges via the SMB5 path.  Advertise only the fixed
5V/3A sink PDO so sources always negotiate a 5V contract the charger
can use.

Signed-off-by: Kumar-Jy <20044626+Kumar-Jy@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-nabu.dts | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-nabu.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-nabu.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-nabu.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-nabu.dts
@@ -688,10 +688,9 @@
 		sink-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 3000,
 					 PDO_FIXED_DUAL_ROLE |
 					 PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM |
-					 PDO_FIXED_DATA_SWAP)
-					 PDO_VAR(5000, 9000, 3000)>;
+					 PDO_FIXED_DATA_SWAP)>;
 
-		op-sink-microwatt = <10000000>;
+		op-sink-microwatt = <15000000>;
 
 		ports {
 			#address-cells = <1>;
-- 
